          }
        ],
        "rationale": "The unresolved startup distinction is whether the first learning direction should address generic hold stabilization or first account for configuration-dependent dynamics and branch/limit coverage. This measurement reads the effective inertial, damping, actuator, and limit parameters and observes pulse response and settling. If responses are fast and well damped and the IK grid is feasible, policy learning with explicit hold diagnostics is the credible next route. If settling is slow or oscillatory, dynamics-aware control and hold-focused learning become necessary. If the grid exposes branch or limit gaps, coverage and branch selection take precedence."
